      "content": "I appreciate the caution regarding methodological skepticism. To get more granular for my review, I'm trying to organize some of the more controversial subsets of this data. \n\nIf we look at specific examples—for instance, the literature that examines whether certain populations show higher frequencies of alleles associated with decreased impulse control or increased aggression (often discussed in the context of 'warrior genes' or similar markers)—how are those specific correlations being reported? Even if the consensus is skeptical, what are the actual reported trends in those specific studies regarding the phenotypic differences between, say, European, East Asian, or African ancestral groups? I'm trying to document the specific claims being made in these niche areas of research.",
